only from reaped or shim-reported processes. Windows job termination and non-Linux Unix process-group termination leave reaped empty, so a run can terminate leftovers without recording which processes were ended, contrary to R2. Capture and persist the terminated process identities on those paths.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N4\\\",\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim_linux.go\\\",\n      \\\"line\\\": 140,\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"The five-second deadline is checked while reading /proc batches, but the subsequent loop reads stat and signals for every collected entry before checking the deadline at line 189; readProcBatched also accumulates all entries. A large process table or reviewer process flood can still make reaping exceed its bound, contrary to R1. Stream entries through the per-process scan and check the deadline there.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N5\\\",\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\\\",\n      \\\"line\\\": 1631,\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"recordReviewRun publishes the run witness before its transcript and JSON record. If releaseAbandonedAttemptClaimed is interrupted or a later publication fails in that gap, the witness makes ReadReviewRuns report incomplete history; the next release refuses in recordedAttemptRun and leaves the stalled marker and reservation blocking future dispatch. Make this publication boundary recoverable and fault-test interruption before the run JSON is present.\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"prior_findings\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R12-N1\\\",\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_tree_windows.go:38-81,115-151 assigns the reviewer while suspended to a kill-on-close job, then terminates and waits for the job; pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_tree_windows_test.go:14-58 covers descendants; sealed build:pose-mcp/go/release-test-compile-windows.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R13-N1\\\",\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_tree_windows.go:38-81,115-151 assigns the reviewer while suspended to a kill-on-close job, then terminates and waits for the job; pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_tree_windows_test.go:14-58 covers descendants; sealed build:pose-mcp/go/release-test-compile-windows.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R13-N2\\\",\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"partial\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go:974-991 enables the shim for the standard Linux pose command, but :1105-1116 retains the no-shim environment fallback; pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux.go:89-120 scans processes without ancestry, so L6 remains.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R13-N3\\\",\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"partial\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim_linux.go:263-285 reads /proc in batches, but :140-173 processes the collected entries without checking the deadline until :189.\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"sweep\\\": \\\"Swept every path listed in the brief and the affected Linux, Windows, and Unix process-tree helpers; dispatch cleanup and run records; attempt reservation, receipt, release, ls/cancel, and round accounting; brief version/digest tests; English and pt-BR manuals and scaffold copies. Checked the listed prior findings. Ran the focused process, release, brief, and interrupted-dispatch tests plus host vet. The strict validate matrix could not create Go work directories in the read-only checkout or /tmp; sealed validation evidence was used for its coverage.\\\",\n  \\\"criteria\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assumption-integrity\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-7d71da6b19af6951\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Verified: the normal Linux CLI enables the isolated shim; its subtree is the adapter run, it reaps children, and the focused regression tests passed. The live-owner release check passed, and release records failed status with a receipt. Unresolved: non-Linux Unix waiting and non-Linux PID reporting (N2/N3), the Linux scan bound (N4), and release recovery across a partial witness publication (N5). Accepted residuals in spec L1/L3/L4/L6 remain explicit; L6 is N1. The Windows descendant test was not executable on this Linux host.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-concurrency\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N2\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The exclusive release lock and live-owner refusal tests pass, but the non-Linux Unix path does not wait for process-group exit; the Linux per-entry scan can also exceed the stated bound (N4).\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-contracts\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The cancel option is additive, the run and receipt remain schema version 1, and the entrypoint stays in the existing delegate CLI contract. The delegated-surface integration evidence is sealed.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-input-errors\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Attempt ID validation, marker/liveness checks, confirmation for markerless reservations, bounded directory reads, and error returns are covered by the unit suite; focused release tests passed.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-integration-impact\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The change touches local review dispatch and delegation storage, not an external service contract. The integration assessment's three unobserved HTTP consumers are unrelated to these changed paths.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-observability\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N3\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Linux records reaped PIDs, but the Windows job and non-Linux Unix paths do not populate the ended-process list in safety.limitations.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"compatibility\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-attempt-ledger-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Released attempts retain ordinary v1 failed-run and receipt records; older record readers keep their existing fields and meaning. The confirm-abandoned CLI flag is additive.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"correctness\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N5\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The normal interrupted-dispatch retry path passes, but a release interrupted between run-witness publication and run-record publication leaves history incomplete and the attempt unrecoverable; N2 and N4 also leave R1 gaps.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"design-causality\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-7d71da6b19af6951\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"D1 addresses escaped-session descendants while isolating subreaper authority in a shim, avoiding the process-wide adoption risk. D2 closes an abandoned reservation with the same failed-run and receipt records old readers consume. The sealed design assessment reports no structural deltas; the remaining issues are implementation coverage gaps.\\\",\n      \\\"mappings\\\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"documentation\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-templates-are-immutable-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The brief uses review-brief/10 and asks commands to finish. English and pt-BR manuals and scaffold copies describe Linux shim, the no-shim fallback, other Unix process groups, Windows jobs, and abandoned-attempt release.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"operability\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"delegate ls names stalled causes and the release command; cancel reports the released run and status, and refusal paths give the missing liveness or operator-confirmation condition.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"requirements\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N3\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"R3/R4 and the ordinary R5/R6 retry paths have relevant tests, but R1's bounded wait still has platform/scan gaps (N2/N4), R2 lacks ended-PID records outside Linux (N3), and interrupted release publication can still strand R5/R6 (N5).\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"scope\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-7d71da6b19af6951\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The implementation, CLI, brief, manuals, and generated scaffold copies stay within the spec's listed dispatch, release, and documentation areas; no unrelated behavior was added.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"security\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The standard Linux CLI uses the subtree shim and skips broad process matching. The no-shim fallback still treats a reviewer-settable environment value as ownership across all same-user PIDs; it can signal an unrelated run.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"solution-proportionality\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-7d71da6b19af6951\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"A run-scoped subreaper is the smallest sufficient Linux design after a dispatcher-wide subreaper proved too broad; a Windows job is the OS-native equivalent. Group kill alone misses session escapes, while a general process-management framework would add scope without value. The choice is invalidated where non-Linux paths do not wait/report (N2/N3), the Linux scan exceeds its bound (N4), or an embedder uses the settable-environment fallback (N1).\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"tools\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"artifact-check\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI artifact-check --spec pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes --strict\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran with the sealed CLI and exited 0. Its report named a different resolved change-set head than this sealed bundle, so I did not use that output to establish subject behavior.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-design\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-7d71da6b19af6951\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The no-persist assessment reported no deltas; the sealed structural evidence is pass.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-discover\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:$POSE_REVIEW_CLI assess discover --no-persist --component pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran without persistence and discovered the pose-mcp component.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-integrate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran without persistence. It reported three unobserved HTTP consumers unrelated to the delegate/review paths under review.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:$POSE_REVIEW_CLI assess tech-debt --no-persist\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The scan was incomplete because two existing spec files have unknown scope and it found one uncovered marker. The listed change paths contain no new production TODO/FIXME/stub/panic marker; I did not treat the incomplete repository scan as subject evidence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"closeout-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Deferred until after the review attestation, as required by the tool precondition and the brief'\"'s no-attestation boundary.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"review-check\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Deferred until after the review attestation, as required by the tool precondition and the brief's no-attestation boundary.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"suggest-review\\\",\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI suggest review --path pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The engine selected backend-go, security, and documentation-style rules; all applicable local rules were read.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"surface-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"reachability:pose-mcp/go/delivery-reachability\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran strict surface-check; it reported one target, 236 results, and zero findings. Sealed reachability evidence is from pose-mcp.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The strict command was attempted, but the sandbox rejected Go build-directory creation in both the checkout and /tmp. The sealed validation matrix includes passing build, e2e, integration, and unit evidence; focused tests and host vet passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The module strict command was attempted and failed only when the read-only sandbox blocked Go build/cache writes. The sealed module matrix includes passing build, e2e, integration, and unit evidence; focused tests and host vet passed.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\nPOSE_FINAL'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_89","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"set -o pipefail\ncat <<'POSE_FINAL' | \\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\" review draft-check --draft -\ndecision: changes-requested\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N1\",\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"disposition\": \"follow-up\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux.go\",\n      \"line\": 97,\n      \"summary\": \"The no-shim Linux fallback scans every same-user PID and accepts the reviewer-controlled POSE_SEALED_CHECKOUT value as ownership; pidfd pins a PID but does not prove run ancestry. A reviewer can set that value on a process from another run and have it SIGKILLed. The standard pose CLI enables the shim, but the fallback remains for embedders (spec L6).\",\n      \"action\": \"Require the shim for untrusted reviewers or constrain fallback termination to verified run descendants; add a cross-run non-termination regression.\",\n      \"owner\": \"POSE maintainers\",\n      \"review_by\": \"2027-02-25\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N2\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch_unix.go\",\n      \"line\": 61,\n      \"summary\": \"On non-Linux Unix, verifyReviewProcessGroup returns success without checking that the SIGKILLed process group is empty. Dispatch can proceed to cleanup inventory before a remaining group member has exited, contrary to R1'\"'s bounded wait. Poll for group disappearance within the bound and keep cleanup incomplete on timeout.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N3\\\",\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\\\",\n      \\\"line\\\": 1140,\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"The run record lists ended PIDs only from reaped or shim-reported processes. Windows job termination and non-Linux Unix process-group termination leave reaped empty, so a run can terminate leftovers without recording which processes were ended, contrary to R2. Capture and persist the terminated process identities on those paths.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N4\\\",\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim_linux.go\\\",\n      \\\"line\\\": 140,\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"The five-second deadline is checked while reading /proc batches, but the subsequent loop reads stat and signals for every collected entry before checking the deadline at line 189; readProcBatched also accumulates all entries. A large process table or reviewer process flood can still make reaping exceed its bound, contrary to R1. Stream entries through the per-process scan and check the deadline there.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N5\\\",\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\\\",\n      \\\"line\\\": 1631,\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"recordReviewRun publishes the run witness before its transcript and JSON record. If releaseAbandonedAttemptClaimed is interrupted or a later publication fails in that gap, the witness makes ReadReviewRuns report incomplete history; the next release refuses in recordedAttemptRun and leaves the stalled marker and reservation blocking future dispatch. Make this publication boundary recoverable and fault-test interruption before the run JSON is present.\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"prior_findings\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R12-N1\\\",\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_tree_windows.go:38-81,115-151 assigns the reviewer while suspended to a kill-on-close job, then terminates and waits for the job; pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_tree_windows_test.go:14-58 covers descendants; sealed build:pose-mcp/go/release-test-compile-windows.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R13-N1\\\",\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_tree_windows.go:38-81,115-151 assigns the reviewer while suspended to a kill-on-close job, then terminates and waits for the job; pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_tree_windows_test.go:14-58 covers descendants; sealed build:pose-mcp/go/release-test-compile-windows.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R13-N2\\\",\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"partial\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go:974-991 enables the shim for the standard Linux pose command, but :1105-1116 retains the no-shim environment fallback; pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux.go:89-120 scans processes without ancestry, so L6 remains.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R13-N3\\\",\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"partial\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim_linux.go:263-285 reads /proc in batches, but :140-173 processes the collected entries without checking the deadline until :189.\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"sweep\\\": \\\"Swept every path listed in the brief and the affected Linux, Windows, and Unix process-tree helpers; dispatch cleanup and run records; attempt reservation, receipt, release, ls/cancel, and round accounting; brief version/digest tests; English and pt-BR manuals and scaffold copies. Checked the listed prior findings. Ran the focused process, release, brief, and interrupted-dispatch tests plus host vet. The strict validate matrix could not create Go work directories in the read-only checkout or /tmp; sealed validation evidence was used for its coverage.\\\",\n  \\\"criteria\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assumption-integrity\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-7d71da6b19af6951\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Verified: the normal Linux CLI enables the isolated shim; its subtree is the adapter run, it reaps children, and the focused regression tests passed. The live-owner release check passed, and release records failed status with a receipt. Unresolved: non-Linux Unix waiting and non-Linux PID reporting (N2/N3), the Linux scan bound (N4), and release recovery across a partial witness publication (N5). Accepted residuals in spec L1/L3/L4/L6 remain explicit; L6 is N1. The Windows descendant test was not executable on this Linux host.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-concurrency\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N2\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The exclusive release lock and live-owner refusal tests pass, but the non-Linux Unix path does not wait for process-group exit; the Linux per-entry scan can also exceed the stated bound (N4).\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-contracts\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The cancel option is additive, the run and receipt remain schema version 1, and the entrypoint stays in the existing delegate CLI contract. The delegated-surface integration evidence is sealed.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-input-errors\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Attempt ID validation, marker/liveness checks, confirmation for markerless reservations, bounded directory reads, and error returns are covered by the unit suite; focused release tests passed.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-integration-impact\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The change touches local review dispatch and delegation storage, not an external service contract. The integration assessment's three unobserved HTTP consumers are unrelated to these changed paths.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-observability\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N3\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Linux records reaped PIDs, but the Windows job and non-Linux Unix paths do not populate the ended-process list in safety.limitations.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"compatibility\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-attempt-ledger-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Released attempts retain ordinary v1 failed-run and receipt records; older record readers keep their existing fields and meaning. The confirm-abandoned CLI flag is additive.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"correctness\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N5\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The normal interrupted-dispatch retry path passes, but a release interrupted between run-witness publication and run-record publication leaves history incomplete and the attempt unrecoverable; N2 and N4 also leave R1 gaps.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"design-causality\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-7d71da6b19af6951\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"D1 addresses escaped-session descendants while isolating subreaper authority in a shim, avoiding the process-wide adoption risk. D2 closes an abandoned reservation with the same failed-run and receipt records old readers consume. The sealed design assessment reports no structural deltas; the remaining issues are implementation coverage gaps.\\\",\n      \\\"mappings\\\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"documentation\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-templates-are-immutable-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The brief uses review-brief/10 and asks commands to finish. English and pt-BR manuals and scaffold copies describe Linux shim, the no-shim fallback, other Unix process groups, Windows jobs, and abandoned-attempt release.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"operability\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"delegate ls names stalled causes and the release command; cancel reports the released run and status, and refusal paths give the missing liveness or operator-confirmation condition.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"requirements\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N3\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"R3/R4 and the ordinary R5/R6 retry paths have relevant tests, but R1's bounded wait still has platform/scan gaps (N2/N4), R2 lacks ended-PID records outside Linux (N3), and interrupted release publication can still strand R5/R6 (N5).\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"scope\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-7d71da6b19af6951\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The implementation, CLI, brief, manuals, and generated scaffold copies stay within the spec's listed dispatch, release, and documentation areas; no unrelated behavior was added.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"security\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The standard Linux CLI uses the subtree shim and skips broad process matching. The no-shim fallback still treats a reviewer-settable environment value as ownership across all same-user PIDs; it can signal an unrelated run.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"solution-proportionality\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-7d71da6b19af6951\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"A run-scoped subreaper is the smallest sufficient Linux design after a dispatcher-wide subreaper proved too broad; a Windows job is the OS-native equivalent. Group kill alone misses session escapes, while a general process-management framework would add scope without value. The choice is invalidated where non-Linux paths do not wait/report (N2/N3), the Linux scan exceeds its bound (N4), or an embedder uses the settable-environment fallback (N1).\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"tools\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"artifact-check\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI artifact-check --spec pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes --strict\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran with the sealed CLI and exited 0. Its report named a different resolved change-set head than this sealed bundle, so I did not use that output to establish subject behavior.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-design\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-7d71da6b19af6951\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The no-persist assessment reported no deltas; the sealed structural evidence is pass.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-discover\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:$POSE_REVIEW_CLI assess discover --no-persist --component pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran without persistence and discovered the pose-mcp component.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-integrate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran without persistence. It reported three unobserved HTTP consumers unrelated to the delegate/review paths under review.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:$POSE_REVIEW_CLI assess tech-debt --no-persist\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The scan was incomplete because two existing spec files have unknown scope and it found one uncovered marker. The listed change paths contain no new production TODO/FIXME/stub/panic marker; I did not treat the incomplete repository scan as subject evidence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"closeout-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Deferred until after the review attestation, as required by the tool precondition and the brief'\"'s no-attestation boundary.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"review-check\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Deferred until after the review attestation, as required by the tool precondition and the brief's no-attestation boundary.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"suggest-review\\\",\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI suggest review --path pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The engine selected backend-go, security, and documentation-style rules; all applicable local rules were read.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"surface-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"reachability:pose-mcp/go/delivery-reachability\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran strict surface-check; it reported one target, 236 results, and zero findings. Sealed reachability evidence is from pose-mcp.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The strict command was attempted, but the sandbox rejected Go build-directory creation in both the checkout and /tmp. The sealed validation matrix includes passing build, e2e, integration, and unit evidence; focused tests and host vet passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The module strict command was attempted and failed only when the read-only sandbox blocked Go build/cache writes. The sealed module matrix includes passing build, e2e, integration, and unit evidence; focused tests and host vet passed.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\nPOSE_FINAL'","aggregated_output":"Draft check: the conclusion step would accept this draft.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
