{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_102","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go | sed -n '8,17p'\nnl -ba pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_tree_windows_test.go | sed -n '1,60p'\ngit status --short\"","aggregated_output":"     8\t\t\"github.com/harne8/pose-mcp/internal/cli\"\n     9\t\t\"github.com/harne8/pose-mcp/internal/pose\"\n    10\t)\n    11\t\n    12\tfunc main() {\n    13\t\tpose.ReviewShimAvailable = true\n    14\t\tif base := filepath.Base(os.Args[0]); base == \"pre-commit\" || base == \"post-merge\" {\n    15\t\t\tos.Exit(cli.HookMain(base, os.Stdout, os.Stderr))\n    16\t\t}\n    17\t\tos.Exit(cli.Main(os.Args[1:], os.Stdout, os.Stderr))\n     1\t//go:build windows\n     2\t\n     3\tpackage pose\n     4\t\n     5\timport (\n     6\t\t\"os/exec\"\n     7\t\t\"testing\"\n     8\t\t\"time\"\n     9\t)\n    10\t\n    11\t// Spec pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes, review round 13,\n    12\t// N1: on Windows the reviewer's tree runs in a job object, and releasing it\n    13\t// ends the descendants the reviewer started.\n    14\tfunc TestTheReviewersJobEndsItsDescendants(t *testing.T) {\n    15\t\t// cmd starts ping as a child and waits for it: both must end with the job.\n    16\t\tcmd := exec.Command(\"cmd\", \"/c\", \"ping -n 60 127.0.0.1 >NUL\")\n    17\t\tprepareReviewProcessTree(cmd)\n    18\t\tif err := cmd.Start(); err != nil {\n    19\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n    20\t\t}\n    21\t\tif err := attachReviewProcessTree(cmd); err != nil {\n    22\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n    23\t\t}\n    24\t\ttime.Sleep(500 * time.Millisecond)\n    25\t\tstarted := time.Now()\n    26\t\tif err := releaseReviewProcessTree(cmd); err != nil {\n    27\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the job did not end its processes: %v\", err)\n    28\t\t}\n    29\t\tdone := make(chan error, 1)\n    30\t\tgo func() { done <- cmd.Wait() }()\n    31\t\tselect {\n    32\t\tcase <-done:\n    33\t\tcase <-time.After(10 * time.Second):\n    34\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"the reviewer outlived its job\")\n    35\t\t}\n    36\t\tif time.Since(started) > 10*time.Second {\n    37\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"ending the job took too long\")\n    38\t\t}\n    39\t}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_103","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"cat <<'POSE_FINAL' | \\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\" review draft-check --draft -\ndecision: changes-requested\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N1\",\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"disposition\": \"follow-up\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux.go\",\n      \"line\": 97,\n      \"summary\": \"The no-shim Linux fallback scans every same-user PID and accepts the reviewer-controlled POSE_SEALED_CHECKOUT value as ownership; pidfd pins a PID but does not prove run ancestry. A process from another run can set that value and be SIGKILLed. The fallback also records a candidate PID before confirming that a signal was delivered. The standard pose CLI enables the shim, but the fallback remains for embedders (spec L6).\",\n      \"action\": \"Require the shim for untrusted reviewers or constrain fallback termination to verified run descendants; record a PID only after confirmed signal delivery and add a cross-run non-termination regression.\",\n      \"owner\": \"POSE maintainers\",\n      \"review_by\": \"2027-02-25\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N2\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch_unix.go\",\n      \"line\": 61,\n      \"summary\": \"On non-Linux Unix, verifyReviewProcessGroup returns success without checking that the SIGKILLed process group is empty. Dispatch can proceed to cleanup inventory before a remaining group member has exited, contrary to R1'\"'s bounded wait. Poll for group disappearance within the bound and keep cleanup incomplete on timeout.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N3\\\",\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\\\",\n      \\\"line\\\": 1140,\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"The run record lists ended PIDs only from reaped or shim-reported processes. Windows job termination and non-Linux Unix process-group termination leave reaped empty, so a run can terminate leftovers without recording which processes were ended, contrary to R2. Capture and persist the terminated process identities on those paths.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N4\\\",\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim_linux.go\\\",\n      \\\"line\\\": 140,\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"The five-second deadline is checked while reading /proc batches, but the subsequent loop reads stats and signals for every collected entry before checking the deadline at line 189; readProcBatched accumulates all entries. The no-shim Linux fallback has the same gap: reviewMarkedProcesses materializes /proc and reads every PID without a deadline (review_reap_linux.go:90-97). A large process table or reviewer process flood can make cleanup exceed its bound, contrary to R1. Stream entries through the per-process scans and check the deadline there.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N5\\\",\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\\\",\n      \\\"line\\\": 1631,\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"recordReviewRun publishes the run witness before its transcript and JSON record. If releaseAbandonedAttemptClaimed is interrupted or a later publication fails in that gap, the witness makes ReadReviewRuns report incomplete history; the next release refuses in recordedAttemptRun (delegation_release.go:169-172) and leaves the stalled marker and reservation blocking future dispatch. Make this publication boundary recoverable and fault-test interruption before the run JSON is present.\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"prior_findings\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R12-N1\\\",\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_tree_windows.go:38-81,115-151 assigns the reviewer while suspended to a kill-on-close job, then terminates and waits for the job; pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_tree_windows_test.go:14-39 covers descendants; sealed build:pose-mcp/go/release-test-compile-windows.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R13-N1\\\",\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_tree_windows.go:38-81,115-151 assigns the reviewer while suspended to a kill-on-close job, then terminates and waits for the job; pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_tree_windows_test.go:14-39 covers descendants; sealed build:pose-mcp/go/release-test-compile-windows.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R13-N2\\\",\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"partial\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go:12-13 enables the shim for the standard pose command, and pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go:974-991 runs it on Linux. The no-shim path remains at pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go:1112-1116; pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux.go:89-120 scans processes without ancestry, so L6 remains.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R13-N3\\\",\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"partial\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim_linux.go:263-285 reads /proc in batches, but :140-173 processes the collected entries without checking the deadline until :189; pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux.go:90-97 also lists and scans without an in-loop deadline.\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"sweep\\\": \\\"Swept every path listed in the brief and the affected Linux, Windows, and Unix process-tree helpers; dispatch cleanup and run records; attempt reservation, receipt, release, ls/cancel, and round accounting; brief version/digest tests; English and pt-BR manuals and scaffold copies. Checked the listed prior findings. Ran the focused process, release, brief, and interrupted-dispatch tests plus host vet. The strict validate matrix could not create Go work directories in the read-only checkout or /tmp; sealed validation evidence was used for its coverage.\\\",\n  \\\"criteria\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assumption-integrity\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-7d71da6b19af6951\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Verified: the normal Linux CLI enables the isolated shim; its subtree is the adapter run, it reaps children, and the focused regression tests passed. The live-owner release check passed, and release records failed status with a receipt. Unresolved: non-Linux Unix waiting and non-Linux PID reporting (N2/N3), the Linux scan bound (N4), and release recovery across a partial witness publication (N5). Accepted residuals in spec L1/L3/L4/L6 remain explicit; L6 is N1. The Windows descendant test was not executable on this Linux host.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-concurrency\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N2\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The exclusive release lock and live-owner refusal tests pass, but the non-Linux Unix path does not wait for process-group exit; the Linux per-entry scan can also exceed the stated bound (N4).\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-contracts\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The cancel option is additive, the run and receipt remain schema version 1, and the entrypoint stays in the existing delegate CLI contract. The delegated-surface integration evidence is sealed.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-input-errors\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Attempt ID validation, marker/liveness checks, confirmation for markerless reservations, bounded directory reads, and error returns are covered by the unit suite; focused release tests passed.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-integration-impact\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The change touches local review dispatch and delegation storage, not an external service contract. The integration assessment's three unobserved HTTP consumers are unrelated to these changed paths.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-observability\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N3\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Linux records reaped PIDs, but the Windows job and non-Linux Unix paths do not populate the ended-process list in safety.limitations.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"compatibility\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-attempt-ledger-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Released attempts retain ordinary v1 failed-run and receipt records; older record readers keep their existing fields and meaning. The confirm-abandoned CLI flag is additive.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"correctness\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N5\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The normal interrupted-dispatch retry path passes, but a release interrupted between run-witness publication and run-record publication leaves history incomplete and the attempt unrecoverable; N2 and N4 also leave R1 gaps.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"design-causality\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-7d71da6b19af6951\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"D1 addresses escaped-session descendants while isolating subreaper authority in a shim, avoiding the process-wide adoption risk. D2 closes an abandoned reservation with the same failed-run and receipt records old readers consume. The sealed design assessment reports no structural deltas; the remaining issues are implementation coverage gaps.\\\",\n      \\\"mappings\\\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"documentation\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-templates-are-immutable-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The brief uses review-brief/10 and asks commands to finish. English and pt-BR manuals and scaffold copies describe Linux shim, the no-shim fallback, other Unix process groups, Windows jobs, and abandoned-attempt release.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"operability\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"delegate ls names stalled causes and the release command; cancel reports the released run and status, and refusal paths give the missing liveness or operator-confirmation condition.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"requirements\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N3\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"R3/R4 and the ordinary R5/R6 retry paths have relevant tests, but R1's bounded wait still has platform/scan gaps (N2/N4), R2 lacks ended-PID records outside Linux (N3), and interrupted release publication can still strand R5/R6 (N5).\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"scope\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-7d71da6b19af6951\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The implementation, CLI, brief, manuals, and generated scaffold copies stay within the spec's listed dispatch, release, and documentation areas; no unrelated behavior was added.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"security\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The standard Linux CLI uses the subtree shim and skips broad process matching. The no-shim fallback still treats a reviewer-settable environment value as ownership across all same-user PIDs; it can signal an unrelated run.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"solution-proportionality\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-7d71da6b19af6951\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"A run-scoped subreaper is the smallest sufficient Linux design after a dispatcher-wide subreaper proved too broad; a Windows job is the OS-native equivalent. Group kill alone misses session escapes, while a general process-management framework would add scope without value. The choice is invalidated where non-Linux paths do not wait/report (N2/N3), the Linux scan exceeds its bound (N4), or an embedder uses the settable-environment fallback (N1).\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"tools\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"artifact-check\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI artifact-check --spec pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes --strict\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran with the sealed CLI and it exited 0. Its report resolved a different change-set head (9636e0ad8e3f6df80ea9b72f2b69bba17b82b936) than this sealed bundle (3e2102bdf778a8af30e5ee38044dfd283488787e), so its 34-claim/40-observed result and warnings were not used to establish this subject'\"'s artifact attribution.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-design\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-7d71da6b19af6951\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The no-persist assessment reported no deltas; the sealed structural evidence is pass.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-discover\\\",\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI assess discover --no-persist --component pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran without persistence and discovered the pose-mcp component.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-integrate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran without persistence. It reported three unobserved HTTP consumers unrelated to the delegate/review paths under review.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:$POSE_REVIEW_CLI assess tech-debt --no-persist\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The scan was incomplete because two existing spec files have unknown scope and it found one uncovered marker. The listed change paths contain no new production TODO/FIXME/stub/panic marker; I did not treat the incomplete repository scan as subject evidence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"closeout-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Deferred until after the review attestation, as required by the tool precondition and the brief'\"'s no-attestation boundary.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"review-check\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Deferred until after the review attestation, as required by the tool precondition and the brief's no-attestation boundary.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"suggest-review\\\",\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI suggest review --path pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The engine selected backend-go, security, and documentation-style rules; all applicable local rules were read.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"surface-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"reachability:pose-mcp/go/delivery-reachability\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran strict surface-check; it reported one target, 236 results, and zero findings. Sealed reachability evidence is from pose-mcp.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The strict command was attempted, but the sandbox rejected Go build-directory creation in both the checkout and /tmp. The sealed validation matrix includes passing build, e2e, integration, and unit evidence; focused tests and host vet passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The module strict command was attempted and failed only when the read-only sandbox blocked Go build/cache writes. The sealed module matrix includes passing build, e2e, integration, and unit evidence; focused tests and host vet passed.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\nPOSE_FINAL'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_103","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"cat <<'POSE_FINAL' | \\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\" review draft-check --draft -\ndecision: changes-requested\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N1\",\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"disposition\": \"follow-up\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux.go\",\n      \"line\": 97,\n      \"summary\": \"The no-shim Linux fallback scans every same-user PID and accepts the reviewer-controlled POSE_SEALED_CHECKOUT value as ownership; pidfd pins a PID but does not prove run ancestry. A process from another run can set that value and be SIGKILLed. The fallback also records a candidate PID before confirming that a signal was delivered. The standard pose CLI enables the shim, but the fallback remains for embedders (spec L6).\",\n      \"action\": \"Require the shim for untrusted reviewers or constrain fallback termination to verified run descendants; record a PID only after confirmed signal delivery and add a cross-run non-termination regression.\",\n      \"owner\": \"POSE maintainers\",\n      \"review_by\": \"2027-02-25\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N2\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch_unix.go\",\n      \"line\": 61,\n      \"summary\": \"On non-Linux Unix, verifyReviewProcessGroup returns success without checking that the SIGKILLed process group is empty. Dispatch can proceed to cleanup inventory before a remaining group member has exited, contrary to R1'\"'s bounded wait. Poll for group disappearance within the bound and keep cleanup incomplete on timeout.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N3\\\",\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\\\",\n      \\\"line\\\": 1140,\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"The run record lists ended PIDs only from reaped or shim-reported processes. Windows job termination and non-Linux Unix process-group termination leave reaped empty, so a run can terminate leftovers without recording which processes were ended, contrary to R2. Capture and persist the terminated process identities on those paths.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N4\\\",\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim_linux.go\\\",\n      \\\"line\\\": 140,\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"The five-second deadline is checked while reading /proc batches, but the subsequent loop reads stats and signals for every collected entry before checking the deadline at line 189; readProcBatched accumulates all entries. The no-shim Linux fallback has the same gap: reviewMarkedProcesses materializes /proc and reads every PID without a deadline (review_reap_linux.go:90-97). A large process table or reviewer process flood can make cleanup exceed its bound, contrary to R1. Stream entries through the per-process scans and check the deadline there.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N5\\\",\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\\\",\n      \\\"line\\\": 1631,\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"recordReviewRun publishes the run witness before its transcript and JSON record. If releaseAbandonedAttemptClaimed is interrupted or a later publication fails in that gap, the witness makes ReadReviewRuns report incomplete history; the next release refuses in recordedAttemptRun (delegation_release.go:169-172) and leaves the stalled marker and reservation blocking future dispatch. Make this publication boundary recoverable and fault-test interruption before the run JSON is present.\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"prior_findings\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R12-N1\\\",\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_tree_windows.go:38-81,115-151 assigns the reviewer while suspended to a kill-on-close job, then terminates and waits for the job; pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_tree_windows_test.go:14-39 covers descendants; sealed build:pose-mcp/go/release-test-compile-windows.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R13-N1\\\",\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_tree_windows.go:38-81,115-151 assigns the reviewer while suspended to a kill-on-close job, then terminates and waits for the job; pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_tree_windows_test.go:14-39 covers descendants; sealed build:pose-mcp/go/release-test-compile-windows.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R13-N2\\\",\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"partial\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go:12-13 enables the shim for the standard pose command, and pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go:974-991 runs it on Linux. The no-shim path remains at pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go:1112-1116; pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux.go:89-120 scans processes without ancestry, so L6 remains.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R13-N3\\\",\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"partial\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim_linux.go:263-285 reads /proc in batches, but :140-173 processes the collected entries without checking the deadline until :189; pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux.go:90-97 also lists and scans without an in-loop deadline.\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"sweep\\\": \\\"Swept every path listed in the brief and the affected Linux, Windows, and Unix process-tree helpers; dispatch cleanup and run records; attempt reservation, receipt, release, ls/cancel, and round accounting; brief version/digest tests; English and pt-BR manuals and scaffold copies. Checked the listed prior findings. Ran the focused process, release, brief, and interrupted-dispatch tests plus host vet. The strict validate matrix could not create Go work directories in the read-only checkout or /tmp; sealed validation evidence was used for its coverage.\\\",\n  \\\"criteria\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assumption-integrity\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-7d71da6b19af6951\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Verified: the normal Linux CLI enables the isolated shim; its subtree is the adapter run, it reaps children, and the focused regression tests passed. The live-owner release check passed, and release records failed status with a receipt. Unresolved: non-Linux Unix waiting and non-Linux PID reporting (N2/N3), the Linux scan bound (N4), and release recovery across a partial witness publication (N5). Accepted residuals in spec L1/L3/L4/L6 remain explicit; L6 is N1. The Windows descendant test was not executable on this Linux host.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-concurrency\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N2\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The exclusive release lock and live-owner refusal tests pass, but the non-Linux Unix path does not wait for process-group exit; the Linux per-entry scan can also exceed the stated bound (N4).\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-contracts\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The cancel option is additive, the run and receipt remain schema version 1, and the entrypoint stays in the existing delegate CLI contract. The delegated-surface integration evidence is sealed.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-input-errors\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Attempt ID validation, marker/liveness checks, confirmation for markerless reservations, bounded directory reads, and error returns are covered by the unit suite; focused release tests passed.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-integration-impact\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The change touches local review dispatch and delegation storage, not an external service contract. The integration assessment's three unobserved HTTP consumers are unrelated to these changed paths.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-observability\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N3\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Linux records reaped PIDs, but the Windows job and non-Linux Unix paths do not populate the ended-process list in safety.limitations.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"compatibility\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-attempt-ledger-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Released attempts retain ordinary v1 failed-run and receipt records; older record readers keep their existing fields and meaning. The confirm-abandoned CLI flag is additive.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"correctness\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N5\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The normal interrupted-dispatch retry path passes, but a release interrupted between run-witness publication and run-record publication leaves history incomplete and the attempt unrecoverable; N2 and N4 also leave R1 gaps.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"design-causality\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-7d71da6b19af6951\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"D1 addresses escaped-session descendants while isolating subreaper authority in a shim, avoiding the process-wide adoption risk. D2 closes an abandoned reservation with the same failed-run and receipt records old readers consume. The sealed design assessment reports no structural deltas; the remaining issues are implementation coverage gaps.\\\",\n      \\\"mappings\\\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"documentation\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-templates-are-immutable-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The brief uses review-brief/10 and asks commands to finish. English and pt-BR manuals and scaffold copies describe Linux shim, the no-shim fallback, other Unix process groups, Windows jobs, and abandoned-attempt release.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"operability\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"delegate ls names stalled causes and the release command; cancel reports the released run and status, and refusal paths give the missing liveness or operator-confirmation condition.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"requirements\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N3\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"R3/R4 and the ordinary R5/R6 retry paths have relevant tests, but R1's bounded wait still has platform/scan gaps (N2/N4), R2 lacks ended-PID records outside Linux (N3), and interrupted release publication can still strand R5/R6 (N5).\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"scope\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-7d71da6b19af6951\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The implementation, CLI, brief, manuals, and generated scaffold copies stay within the spec's listed dispatch, release, and documentation areas; no unrelated behavior was added.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"security\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The standard Linux CLI uses the subtree shim and skips broad process matching. The no-shim fallback still treats a reviewer-settable environment value as ownership across all same-user PIDs; it can signal an unrelated run.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"solution-proportionality\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-7d71da6b19af6951\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"A run-scoped subreaper is the smallest sufficient Linux design after a dispatcher-wide subreaper proved too broad; a Windows job is the OS-native equivalent. Group kill alone misses session escapes, while a general process-management framework would add scope without value. The choice is invalidated where non-Linux paths do not wait/report (N2/N3), the Linux scan exceeds its bound (N4), or an embedder uses the settable-environment fallback (N1).\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"tools\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"artifact-check\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI artifact-check --spec pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes --strict\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran with the sealed CLI and it exited 0. Its report resolved a different change-set head (9636e0ad8e3f6df80ea9b72f2b69bba17b82b936) than this sealed bundle (3e2102bdf778a8af30e5ee38044dfd283488787e), so its 34-claim/40-observed result and warnings were not used to establish this subject'\"'s artifact attribution.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-design\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-7d71da6b19af6951\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The no-persist assessment reported no deltas; the sealed structural evidence is pass.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-discover\\\",\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI assess discover --no-persist --component pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran without persistence and discovered the pose-mcp component.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-integrate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran without persistence. It reported three unobserved HTTP consumers unrelated to the delegate/review paths under review.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:$POSE_REVIEW_CLI assess tech-debt --no-persist\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The scan was incomplete because two existing spec files have unknown scope and it found one uncovered marker. The listed change paths contain no new production TODO/FIXME/stub/panic marker; I did not treat the incomplete repository scan as subject evidence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"closeout-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Deferred until after the review attestation, as required by the tool precondition and the brief'\"'s no-attestation boundary.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"review-check\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Deferred until after the review attestation, as required by the tool precondition and the brief's no-attestation boundary.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"suggest-review\\\",\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI suggest review --path pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The engine selected backend-go, security, and documentation-style rules; all applicable local rules were read.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"surface-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"reachability:pose-mcp/go/delivery-reachability\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran strict surface-check; it reported one target, 236 results, and zero findings. Sealed reachability evidence is from pose-mcp.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The strict command was attempted, but the sandbox rejected Go build-directory creation in both the checkout and /tmp. The sealed validation matrix includes passing build, e2e, integration, and unit evidence; focused tests and host vet passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The module strict command was attempted and failed only when the read-only sandbox blocked Go build/cache writes. The sealed module matrix includes passing build, e2e, integration, and unit evidence; focused tests and host vet passed.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\nPOSE_FINAL'","aggregated_output":"Draft check: the conclusion step would accept this draft.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_104","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"cat <<'POSE_FINAL' | \\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\" review draft-check --draft -\ndecision: changes-requested\n\n## Findings\n\n- **N1 — low, follow-up:** The no-shim Linux fallback trusts a reviewer-settable environment value as ownership across same-user PIDs, and records candidate PIDs before confirming signal delivery. See [review_reap_linux.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-2592453193/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux.go:97).\n- **N2 — medium, blocker:** Non-Linux Unix dispatch treats SIGKILL delivery as proof the process group is gone and may begin cleanup without waiting. See [review_dispatch_unix.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-2592453193/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch_unix.go:61).\n- **N3 — medium, blocker:** Windows job termination and non-Linux Unix group termination do not populate the ended-process list, so the run record does not identify leftovers it ended. See [review_dispatch.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-2592453193/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go:1140).\n- **N4 — medium, blocker:** Linux process scans check the deadline between batches but not during per-process inspection; both the shim and no-shim fallback can exceed the cleanup bound. See [review_shim_linux.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-2592453193/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim_linux.go:140) and [review_reap_linux.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-2592453193/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux.go:90).\n- **N5 — medium, blocker:** Publishing the run witness before the transcript and JSON record creates a state the abandoned-attempt release cannot recover. See [review_dispatch.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-2592453193/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go:1631) and [delegation_release.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-2592453193/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release.go:169).\n\n## Criteria\n\n| Criterion | Result | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| assumption-integrity | passed | structure:design-7d71da6b19af6951 |\n| backend-concurrency | failed | N2 |\n| backend-contracts | passed | integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration |\n| backend-input-errors | passed | unit:pose-mcp/go/test |\n| backend-integration-impact | passed | integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration |\n| backend-observability | failed | N3 |\n| compatibility | passed | integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-attempt-ledger-integration |\n| correctness | failed | N5 |\n| design-causality | passed | structure:design-7d71da6b19af6951 |\n| documentation | passed | integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-templates-are-immutable-integration |\n| operability | passed | integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration |\n| requirements | failed | N3 |\n| scope | passed | structure:design-7d71da6b19af6951 |\n| security | failed | N1 |\n| solution-proportionality | passed | structure:design-7d71da6b19af6951 |\n\n## Checks and review limits\n\nThe focused process, release, brief, and interrupted-dispatch Go tests passed, as did host vet. The strict validation commands could not create Go build/cache directories in the read-only checkout or /tmp; the sealed validation matrix supplies build, e2e, integration, and unit evidence. The Windows job test was compiled for Windows but not run on this Linux host.\n\nThe required artifact-check command exited 0 but resolved change-set head 9636e0ad8e3f6df80ea9b72f2b69bba17b82b936, rather than the reviewed head 3e2102bdf778a8af30e5ee38044dfd283488787e, so its claims and warnings do not establish this bundle'\"'s attribution. Closeout-check and review-check are deferred because their precondition is a completed attestation, which this review must not record. Tech-debt assessment was incomplete because of two existing specs with unknown scope and one uncovered marker.\n\nPrior findings: R12-N1 and R13-N1 are fixed by the Windows kill-on-close job; R13-N2 and R13-N3 are partial, with evidence recorded in the draft. The review draft checker accepted this conclusion. No repository changes were made.\n\n\"'```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N1\",\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"disposition\": \"follow-up\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux.go\",\n      \"line\": 97,\n      \"summary\": \"The no-shim Linux fallback scans every same-user PID and accepts the reviewer-controlled POSE_SEALED_CHECKOUT value as ownership; pidfd pins a PID but does not prove run ancestry. A process from another run can set that value and be SIGKILLed. The fallback also records a candidate PID before confirming that a signal was delivered. The standard pose CLI enables the shim, but the fallback remains for embedders (spec L6).\",\n      \"action\": \"Require the shim for untrusted reviewers or constrain fallback termination to verified run descendants; record a PID only after confirmed signal delivery and add a cross-run non-termination regression.\",\n      \"owner\": \"POSE maintainers\",\n      \"review_by\": \"2027-02-25\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N2\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch_unix.go\",\n      \"line\": 61,\n      \"summary\": \"On non-Linux Unix, verifyReviewProcessGroup returns success without checking that the SIGKILLed process group is empty. Dispatch can proceed to cleanup inventory before a remaining group member has exited, contrary to R1'\"'s bounded wait. Poll for group disappearance within the bound and keep cleanup incomplete on timeout.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N3\\\",\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\\\",\n      \\\"line\\\": 1140,\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"The run record lists ended PIDs only from reaped or shim-reported processes. Windows job termination and non-Linux Unix process-group termination leave reaped empty, so a run can terminate leftovers without recording which processes were ended, contrary to R2. Capture and persist the terminated process identities on those paths.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N4\\\",\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim_linux.go\\\",\n      \\\"line\\\": 140,\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"The five-second deadline is checked while reading /proc batches, but the subsequent loop reads stats and signals for every collected entry before checking the deadline at line 189; readProcBatched accumulates all entries. The no-shim Linux fallback has the same gap: reviewMarkedProcesses materializes /proc and reads every PID without a deadline (review_reap_linux.go:90-97). A large process table or reviewer process flood can make cleanup exceed its bound, contrary to R1. Stream entries through the per-process scans and check the deadline there.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N5\\\",\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\\\",\n      \\\"line\\\": 1631,\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"recordReviewRun publishes the run witness before its transcript and JSON record. If releaseAbandonedAttemptClaimed is interrupted or a later publication fails in that gap, the witness makes ReadReviewRuns report incomplete history; the next release refuses in recordedAttemptRun (delegation_release.go:169-172) and leaves the stalled marker and reservation blocking future dispatch. Make this publication boundary recoverable and fault-test interruption before the run JSON is present.\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"prior_findings\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R12-N1\\\",\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_tree_windows.go:38-81,115-151 assigns the reviewer while suspended to a kill-on-close job, then terminates and waits for the job; pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_tree_windows_test.go:14-39 covers descendants; sealed build:pose-mcp/go/release-test-compile-windows.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R13-N1\\\",\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_tree_windows.go:38-81,115-151 assigns the reviewer while suspended to a kill-on-close job, then terminates and waits for the job; pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_tree_windows_test.go:14-39 covers descendants; sealed build:pose-mcp/go/release-test-compile-windows.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R13-N2\\\",\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"partial\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go:12-13 enables the shim for the standard pose command, and pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go:974-991 runs it on Linux. The no-shim path remains at pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go:1112-1116; pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux.go:89-120 scans processes without ancestry, so L6 remains.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R13-N3\\\",\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"partial\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim_linux.go:263-285 reads /proc in batches, but :140-173 processes the collected entries without checking the deadline until :189; pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux.go:90-97 also lists and scans without an in-loop deadline.\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"sweep\\\": \\\"Swept every path listed in the brief and the affected Linux, Windows, and Unix process-tree helpers; dispatch cleanup and run records; attempt reservation, receipt, release, ls/cancel, and round accounting; brief version/digest tests; English and pt-BR manuals and scaffold copies. Checked the listed prior findings. Ran the focused process, release, brief, and interrupted-dispatch tests plus host vet. The strict validate matrix could not create Go work directories in the read-only checkout or /tmp; sealed validation evidence was used for its coverage.\\\",\n  \\\"criteria\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assumption-integrity\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-7d71da6b19af6951\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Verified: the normal Linux CLI enables the isolated shim; its subtree is the adapter run, it reaps children, and the focused regression tests passed. The live-owner release check passed, and release records failed status with a receipt. Unresolved: non-Linux Unix waiting and non-Linux PID reporting (N2/N3), the Linux scan bound (N4), and release recovery across a partial witness publication (N5). Accepted residuals in spec L1/L3/L4/L6 remain explicit; L6 is N1. The Windows descendant test was not executable on this Linux host.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-concurrency\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N2\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The exclusive release lock and live-owner refusal tests pass, but the non-Linux Unix path does not wait for process-group exit; the Linux per-entry scan can also exceed the stated bound (N4).\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-contracts\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The cancel option is additive, the run and receipt remain schema version 1, and the entrypoint stays in the existing delegate CLI contract. The delegated-surface integration evidence is sealed.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-input-errors\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Attempt ID validation, marker/liveness checks, confirmation for markerless reservations, bounded directory reads, and error returns are covered by the unit suite; focused release tests passed.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-integration-impact\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The change touches local review dispatch and delegation storage, not an external service contract. The integration assessment's three unobserved HTTP consumers are unrelated to these changed paths.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-observability\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N3\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Linux records reaped PIDs, but the Windows job and non-Linux Unix paths do not populate the ended-process list in safety.limitations.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"compatibility\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-attempt-ledger-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Released attempts retain ordinary v1 failed-run and receipt records; older record readers keep their existing fields and meaning. The confirm-abandoned CLI flag is additive.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"correctness\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N5\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The normal interrupted-dispatch retry path passes, but a release interrupted between run-witness publication and run-record publication leaves history incomplete and the attempt unrecoverable; N2 and N4 also leave R1 gaps.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"design-causality\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-7d71da6b19af6951\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"D1 addresses escaped-session descendants while isolating subreaper authority in a shim, avoiding the process-wide adoption risk. D2 closes an abandoned reservation with the same failed-run and receipt records old readers consume. The sealed design assessment reports no structural deltas; the remaining issues are implementation coverage gaps.\\\",\n      \\\"mappings\\\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"documentation\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-templates-are-immutable-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The brief uses review-brief/10 and asks commands to finish. English and pt-BR manuals and scaffold copies describe Linux shim, the no-shim fallback, other Unix process groups, Windows jobs, and abandoned-attempt release.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"operability\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"delegate ls names stalled causes and the release command; cancel reports the released run and status, and refusal paths give the missing liveness or operator-confirmation condition.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"requirements\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N3\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"R3/R4 and the ordinary R5/R6 retry paths have relevant tests, but R1's bounded wait still has platform/scan gaps (N2/N4), R2 lacks ended-PID records outside Linux (N3), and interrupted release publication can still strand R5/R6 (N5).\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"scope\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-7d71da6b19af6951\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The implementation, CLI, brief, manuals, and generated scaffold copies stay within the spec's listed dispatch, release, and documentation areas; no unrelated behavior was added.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"security\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The standard Linux CLI uses the subtree shim and skips broad process matching. The no-shim fallback still treats a reviewer-settable environment value as ownership across all same-user PIDs; it can signal an unrelated run.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"solution-proportionality\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-7d71da6b19af6951\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"A run-scoped subreaper is the smallest sufficient Linux design after a dispatcher-wide subreaper proved too broad; a Windows job is the OS-native equivalent. Group kill alone misses session escapes, while a general process-management framework would add scope without value. The choice is invalidated where non-Linux paths do not wait/report (N2/N3), the Linux scan exceeds its bound (N4), or an embedder uses the settable-environment fallback (N1).\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"tools\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"artifact-check\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI artifact-check --spec pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes --strict\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran with the sealed CLI and it exited 0. Its report resolved a different change-set head (9636e0ad8e3f6df80ea9b72f2b69bba17b82b936) than this sealed bundle (3e2102bdf778a8af30e5ee38044dfd283488787e), so its 34-claim/40-observed result and warnings were not used to establish this subject'\"'s artifact attribution.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-design\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-7d71da6b19af6951\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The no-persist assessment reported no deltas; the sealed structural evidence is pass.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-discover\\\",\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI assess discover --no-persist --component pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran without persistence and discovered the pose-mcp component.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-integrate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran without persistence. It reported three unobserved HTTP consumers unrelated to the delegate/review paths under review.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:$POSE_REVIEW_CLI assess tech-debt --no-persist\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The scan was incomplete because two existing spec files have unknown scope and it found one uncovered marker. The listed change paths contain no new production TODO/FIXME/stub/panic marker; I did not treat the incomplete repository scan as subject evidence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"closeout-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Deferred until after the review attestation, as required by the tool precondition and the brief'\"'s no-attestation boundary.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"review-check\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Deferred until after the review attestation, as required by the tool precondition and the brief's no-attestation boundary.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"suggest-review\\\",\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI suggest review --path pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The engine selected backend-go, security, and documentation-style rules; all applicable local rules were read.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"surface-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"reachability:pose-mcp/go/delivery-reachability\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran strict surface-check; it reported one target, 236 results, and zero findings. Sealed reachability evidence is from pose-mcp.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The strict command was attempted, but the sandbox rejected Go build-directory creation in both the checkout and /tmp. The sealed validation matrix includes passing build, e2e, integration, and unit evidence; focused tests and host vet passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The module strict command was attempted and failed only when the read-only sandbox blocked Go build/cache writes. The sealed module matrix includes passing build, e2e, integration, and unit evidence; focused tests and host vet passed.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\nPOSE_FINAL'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_104","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"cat <<'POSE_FINAL' | \\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\" review draft-check --draft -\ndecision: changes-requested\n\n## Findings\n\n- **N1 — low, follow-up:** The no-shim Linux fallback trusts a reviewer-settable environment value as ownership across same-user PIDs, and records candidate PIDs before confirming signal delivery. See [review_reap_linux.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-2592453193/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux.go:97).\n- **N2 — medium, blocker:** Non-Linux Unix dispatch treats SIGKILL delivery as proof the process group is gone and may begin cleanup without waiting. See [review_dispatch_unix.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-2592453193/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch_unix.go:61).\n- **N3 — medium, blocker:** Windows job termination and non-Linux Unix group termination do not populate the ended-process list, so the run record does not identify leftovers it ended. See [review_dispatch.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-2592453193/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go:1140).\n- **N4 — medium, blocker:** Linux process scans check the deadline between batches but not during per-process inspection; both the shim and no-shim fallback can exceed the cleanup bound. See [review_shim_linux.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-2592453193/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim_linux.go:140) and [review_reap_linux.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-2592453193/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux.go:90).\n- **N5 — medium, blocker:** Publishing the run witness before the transcript and JSON record creates a state the abandoned-attempt release cannot recover. See [review_dispatch.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-2592453193/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go:1631) and [delegation_release.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-2592453193/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release.go:169).\n\n## Criteria\n\n| Criterion | Result | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| assumption-integrity | passed | structure:design-7d71da6b19af6951 |\n| backend-concurrency | failed | N2 |\n| backend-contracts | passed | integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration |\n| backend-input-errors | passed | unit:pose-mcp/go/test |\n| backend-integration-impact | passed | integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration |\n| backend-observability | failed | N3 |\n| compatibility | passed | integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-attempt-ledger-integration |\n| correctness | failed | N5 |\n| design-causality | passed | structure:design-7d71da6b19af6951 |\n| documentation | passed | integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-templates-are-immutable-integration |\n| operability | passed | integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration |\n| requirements | failed | N3 |\n| scope | passed | structure:design-7d71da6b19af6951 |\n| security | failed | N1 |\n| solution-proportionality | passed | structure:design-7d71da6b19af6951 |\n\n## Checks and review limits\n\nThe focused process, release, brief, and interrupted-dispatch Go tests passed, as did host vet. The strict validation commands could not create Go build/cache directories in the read-only checkout or /tmp; the sealed validation matrix supplies build, e2e, integration, and unit evidence. The Windows job test was compiled for Windows but not run on this Linux host.\n\nThe required artifact-check command exited 0 but resolved change-set head 9636e0ad8e3f6df80ea9b72f2b69bba17b82b936, rather than the reviewed head 3e2102bdf778a8af30e5ee38044dfd283488787e, so its claims and warnings do not establish this bundle'\"'s attribution. Closeout-check and review-check are deferred because their precondition is a completed attestation, which this review must not record. Tech-debt assessment was incomplete because of two existing specs with unknown scope and one uncovered marker.\n\nPrior findings: R12-N1 and R13-N1 are fixed by the Windows kill-on-close job; R13-N2 and R13-N3 are partial, with evidence recorded in the draft. The review draft checker accepted this conclusion. No repository changes were made.\n\n\"'```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N1\",\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"disposition\": \"follow-up\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux.go\",\n      \"line\": 97,\n      \"summary\": \"The no-shim Linux fallback scans every same-user PID and accepts the reviewer-controlled POSE_SEALED_CHECKOUT value as ownership; pidfd pins a PID but does not prove run ancestry. A process from another run can set that value and be SIGKILLed. The fallback also records a candidate PID before confirming that a signal was delivered. The standard pose CLI enables the shim, but the fallback remains for embedders (spec L6).\",\n      \"action\": \"Require the shim for untrusted reviewers or constrain fallback termination to verified run descendants; record a PID only after confirmed signal delivery and add a cross-run non-termination regression.\",\n      \"owner\": \"POSE maintainers\",\n      \"review_by\": \"2027-02-25\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N2\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch_unix.go\",\n      \"line\": 61,\n      \"summary\": \"On non-Linux Unix, verifyReviewProcessGroup returns success without checking that the SIGKILLed process group is empty. Dispatch can proceed to cleanup inventory before a remaining group member has exited, contrary to R1'\"'s bounded wait. Poll for group disappearance within the bound and keep cleanup incomplete on timeout.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N3\\\",\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\\\",\n      \\\"line\\\": 1140,\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"The run record lists ended PIDs only from reaped or shim-reported processes. Windows job termination and non-Linux Unix process-group termination leave reaped empty, so a run can terminate leftovers without recording which processes were ended, contrary to R2. Capture and persist the terminated process identities on those paths.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N4\\\",\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim_linux.go\\\",\n      \\\"line\\\": 140,\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"The five-second deadline is checked while reading /proc batches, but the subsequent loop reads stats and signals for every collected entry before checking the deadline at line 189; readProcBatched accumulates all entries. The no-shim Linux fallback has the same gap: reviewMarkedProcesses materializes /proc and reads every PID without a deadline (review_reap_linux.go:90-97). A large process table or reviewer process flood can make cleanup exceed its bound, contrary to R1. Stream entries through the per-process scans and check the deadline there.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N5\\\",\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\\\",\n      \\\"line\\\": 1631,\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"recordReviewRun publishes the run witness before its transcript and JSON record. If releaseAbandonedAttemptClaimed is interrupted or a later publication fails in that gap, the witness makes ReadReviewRuns report incomplete history; the next release refuses in recordedAttemptRun (delegation_release.go:169-172) and leaves the stalled marker and reservation blocking future dispatch. Make this publication boundary recoverable and fault-test interruption before the run JSON is present.\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"prior_findings\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R12-N1\\\",\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_tree_windows.go:38-81,115-151 assigns the reviewer while suspended to a kill-on-close job, then terminates and waits for the job; pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_tree_windows_test.go:14-39 covers descendants; sealed build:pose-mcp/go/release-test-compile-windows.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R13-N1\\\",\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_tree_windows.go:38-81,115-151 assigns the reviewer while suspended to a kill-on-close job, then terminates and waits for the job; pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_tree_windows_test.go:14-39 covers descendants; sealed build:pose-mcp/go/release-test-compile-windows.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R13-N2\\\",\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"partial\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go:12-13 enables the shim for the standard pose command, and pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go:974-991 runs it on Linux. The no-shim path remains at pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go:1112-1116; pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux.go:89-120 scans processes without ancestry, so L6 remains.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R13-N3\\\",\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"partial\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim_linux.go:263-285 reads /proc in batches, but :140-173 processes the collected entries without checking the deadline until :189; pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux.go:90-97 also lists and scans without an in-loop deadline.\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"sweep\\\": \\\"Swept every path listed in the brief and the affected Linux, Windows, and Unix process-tree helpers; dispatch cleanup and run records; attempt reservation, receipt, release, ls/cancel, and round accounting; brief version/digest tests; English and pt-BR manuals and scaffold copies. Checked the listed prior findings. Ran the focused process, release, brief, and interrupted-dispatch tests plus host vet. The strict validate matrix could not create Go work directories in the read-only checkout or /tmp; sealed validation evidence was used for its coverage.\\\",\n  \\\"criteria\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assumption-integrity\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-7d71da6b19af6951\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Verified: the normal Linux CLI enables the isolated shim; its subtree is the adapter run, it reaps children, and the focused regression tests passed. The live-owner release check passed, and release records failed status with a receipt. Unresolved: non-Linux Unix waiting and non-Linux PID reporting (N2/N3), the Linux scan bound (N4), and release recovery across a partial witness publication (N5). Accepted residuals in spec L1/L3/L4/L6 remain explicit; L6 is N1. The Windows descendant test was not executable on this Linux host.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-concurrency\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N2\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The exclusive release lock and live-owner refusal tests pass, but the non-Linux Unix path does not wait for process-group exit; the Linux per-entry scan can also exceed the stated bound (N4).\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-contracts\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The cancel option is additive, the run and receipt remain schema version 1, and the entrypoint stays in the existing delegate CLI contract. The delegated-surface integration evidence is sealed.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-input-errors\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Attempt ID validation, marker/liveness checks, confirmation for markerless reservations, bounded directory reads, and error returns are covered by the unit suite; focused release tests passed.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-integration-impact\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The change touches local review dispatch and delegation storage, not an external service contract. The integration assessment's three unobserved HTTP consumers are unrelated to these changed paths.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-observability\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N3\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Linux records reaped PIDs, but the Windows job and non-Linux Unix paths do not populate the ended-process list in safety.limitations.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"compatibility\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-attempt-ledger-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Released attempts retain ordinary v1 failed-run and receipt records; older record readers keep their existing fields and meaning. The confirm-abandoned CLI flag is additive.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"correctness\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N5\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The normal interrupted-dispatch retry path passes, but a release interrupted between run-witness publication and run-record publication leaves history incomplete and the attempt unrecoverable; N2 and N4 also leave R1 gaps.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"design-causality\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-7d71da6b19af6951\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"D1 addresses escaped-session descendants while isolating subreaper authority in a shim, avoiding the process-wide adoption risk. D2 closes an abandoned reservation with the same failed-run and receipt records old readers consume. The sealed design assessment reports no structural deltas; the remaining issues are implementation coverage gaps.\\\",\n      \\\"mappings\\\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"documentation\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-templates-are-immutable-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The brief uses review-brief/10 and asks commands to finish. English and pt-BR manuals and scaffold copies describe Linux shim, the no-shim fallback, other Unix process groups, Windows jobs, and abandoned-attempt release.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"operability\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"delegate ls names stalled causes and the release command; cancel reports the released run and status, and refusal paths give the missing liveness or operator-confirmation condition.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"requirements\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N3\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"R3/R4 and the ordinary R5/R6 retry paths have relevant tests, but R1's bounded wait still has platform/scan gaps (N2/N4), R2 lacks ended-PID records outside Linux (N3), and interrupted release publication can still strand R5/R6 (N5).\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"scope\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-7d71da6b19af6951\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The implementation, CLI, brief, manuals, and generated scaffold copies stay within the spec's listed dispatch, release, and documentation areas; no unrelated behavior was added.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"security\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The standard Linux CLI uses the subtree shim and skips broad process matching. The no-shim fallback still treats a reviewer-settable environment value as ownership across all same-user PIDs; it can signal an unrelated run.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"solution-proportionality\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-7d71da6b19af6951\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"A run-scoped subreaper is the smallest sufficient Linux design after a dispatcher-wide subreaper proved too broad; a Windows job is the OS-native equivalent. Group kill alone misses session escapes, while a general process-management framework would add scope without value. The choice is invalidated where non-Linux paths do not wait/report (N2/N3), the Linux scan exceeds its bound (N4), or an embedder uses the settable-environment fallback (N1).\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"tools\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"artifact-check\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI artifact-check --spec pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes --strict\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran with the sealed CLI and it exited 0. Its report resolved a different change-set head (9636e0ad8e3f6df80ea9b72f2b69bba17b82b936) than this sealed bundle (3e2102bdf778a8af30e5ee38044dfd283488787e), so its 34-claim/40-observed result and warnings were not used to establish this subject'\"'s artifact attribution.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-design\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-7d71da6b19af6951\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The no-persist assessment reported no deltas; the sealed structural evidence is pass.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-discover\\\",\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI assess discover --no-persist --component pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran without persistence and discovered the pose-mcp component.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-integrate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran without persistence. It reported three unobserved HTTP consumers unrelated to the delegate/review paths under review.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:$POSE_REVIEW_CLI assess tech-debt --no-persist\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The scan was incomplete because two existing spec files have unknown scope and it found one uncovered marker. The listed change paths contain no new production TODO/FIXME/stub/panic marker; I did not treat the incomplete repository scan as subject evidence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"closeout-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Deferred until after the review attestation, as required by the tool precondition and the brief'\"'s no-attestation boundary.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"review-check\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Deferred until after the review attestation, as required by the tool precondition and the brief's no-attestation boundary.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"suggest-review\\\",\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI suggest review --path pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The engine selected backend-go, security, and documentation-style rules; all applicable local rules were read.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"surface-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"reachability:pose-mcp/go/delivery-reachability\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran strict surface-check; it reported one target, 236 results, and zero findings. Sealed reachability evidence is from pose-mcp.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The strict command was attempted, but the sandbox rejected Go build-directory creation in both the checkout and /tmp. The sealed validation matrix includes passing build, e2e, integration, and unit evidence; focused tests and host vet passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The module strict command was attempted and failed only when the read-only sandbox blocked Go build/cache writes. The sealed module matrix includes passing build, e2e, integration, and unit evidence; focused tests and host vet passed.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\nPOSE_FINAL'","aggregated_output":"Draft check: the conclusion step would accept this draft.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_105","type":"agent_message","text":"decision: changes-requested\n\n## Findings\n\n- **N1 — low, follow-up:** The no-shim Linux fallback trusts a reviewer-settable environment value as ownership across same-user PIDs, and records candidate PIDs before confirming signal delivery. See [review_reap_linux.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-2592453193/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux.go:97).\n- **N2 — medium, blocker:** Non-Linux Unix dispatch treats SIGKILL delivery as proof the process group is gone and may begin cleanup without waiting. See [review_dispatch_unix.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-2592453193/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch_unix.go:61).\n- **N3 — medium, blocker:** Windows job termination and non-Linux Unix group termination do not populate the ended-process list, so the run record does not identify leftovers it ended. See [review_dispatch.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-2592453193/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go:1140).\n- **N4 — medium, blocker:** Linux process scans check the deadline between batches but not during per-process inspection; both the shim and no-shim fallback can exceed the cleanup bound. See [review_shim_linux.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-2592453193/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim_linux.go:140) and [review_reap_linux.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-2592453193/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux.go:90).\n- **N5 — medium, blocker:** Publishing the run witness before the transcript and JSON record creates a state the abandoned-attempt release cannot recover. See [review_dispatch.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-2592453193/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go:1631) and [delegation_release.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-2592453193/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release.go:169).\n\n## Criteria\n\n| Criterion | Result | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| assumption-integrity | passed | structure:design-7d71da6b19af6951 |\n| backend-concurrency | failed | N2 |\n| backend-contracts | passed | integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration |\n| backend-input-errors | passed | unit:pose-mcp/go/test |\n| backend-integration-impact | passed | integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration |\n| backend-observability | failed | N3 |\n| compatibility | passed | integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-attempt-ledger-integration |\n| correctness | failed | N5 |\n| design-causality | passed | structure:design-7d71da6b19af6951 |\n| documentation | passed | integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-templates-are-immutable-integration |\n| operability | passed | integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration |\n| requirements | failed | N3 |\n| scope | passed | structure:design-7d71da6b19af6951 |\n| security | failed | N1 |\n| solution-proportionality | passed | structure:design-7d71da6b19af6951 |\n\n## Checks and review limits\n\nThe focused process, release, brief, and interrupted-dispatch Go tests passed, as did host vet. The strict validation commands could not create Go build/cache directories in the read-only checkout or `/tmp`; the sealed validation matrix supplies build, e2e, integration, and unit evidence. The Windows job test was compiled for Windows but not run on this Linux host.\n\nThe required artifact-check command exited 0 but resolved change-set head `9636e0ad8e3f6df80ea9b72f2b69bba17b82b936`, rather than the reviewed head `3e2102bdf778a8af30e5ee38044dfd283488787e`, so its claims and warnings do not establish this bundle's attribution. Closeout-check and review-check are deferred because their precondition is a completed attestation, which this review must not record. Tech-debt assessment was incomplete because of two existing specs with unknown scope and one uncovered marker.\n\nPrior findings: R12-N1 and R13-N1 are fixed by the Windows kill-on-close job; R13-N2 and R13-N3 are partial, with evidence recorded in the draft. The review draft checker accepted this conclusion. No repository changes were made.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N1\",\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"disposition\": \"follow-up\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux.go\",\n      \"line\": 97,\n      \"summary\": \"The no-shim Linux fallback scans every same-user PID and accepts the reviewer-controlled POSE_SEALED_CHECKOUT value as ownership; pidfd pins a PID but does not prove run ancestry. A process from another run can set that value and be SIGKILLed. The fallback also records a candidate PID before confirming that a signal was delivered. The standard pose CLI enables the shim, but the fallback remains for embedders (spec L6).\",\n      \"action\": \"Require the shim for untrusted reviewers or constrain fallback termination to verified run descendants; record a PID only after confirmed signal delivery and add a cross-run non-termination regression.\",\n      \"owner\": \"POSE maintainers\",\n      \"review_by\": \"2027-02-25\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N2\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch_unix.go\",\n      \"line\": 61,\n      \"summary\": \"On non-Linux Unix, verifyReviewProcessGroup returns success without checking that the SIGKILLed process group is empty. Dispatch can proceed to cleanup inventory before a remaining group member has exited, contrary to R1's bounded wait. Poll for group disappearance within the bound and keep cleanup incomplete on timeout.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N3\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\",\n      \"line\": 1140,\n      \"summary\": \"The run record lists ended PIDs only from reaped or shim-reported processes. Windows job termination and non-Linux Unix process-group termination leave reaped empty, so a run can terminate leftovers without recording which processes were ended, contrary to R2. Capture and persist the terminated process identities on those paths.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N4\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim_linux.go\",\n      \"line\": 140,\n      \"summary\": \"The five-second deadline is checked while reading /proc batches, but the subsequent loop reads stats and signals for every collected entry before checking the deadline at line 189; readProcBatched accumulates all entries. The no-shim Linux fallback has the same gap: reviewMarkedProcesses materializes /proc and reads every PID without a deadline (review_reap_linux.go:90-97). A large process table or reviewer process flood can make cleanup exceed its bound, contrary to R1. Stream entries through the per-process scans and check the deadline there.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N5\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\",\n      \"line\": 1631,\n      \"summary\": \"recordReviewRun publishes the run witness before its transcript and JSON record. If releaseAbandonedAttemptClaimed is interrupted or a later publication fails in that gap, the witness makes ReadReviewRuns report incomplete history; the next release refuses in recordedAttemptRun (delegation_release.go:169-172) and leaves the stalled marker and reservation blocking future dispatch. Make this publication boundary recoverable and fault-test interruption before the run JSON is present.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"prior_findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R12-N1\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_tree_windows.go:38-81,115-151 assigns the reviewer while suspended to a kill-on-close job, then terminates and waits for the job; pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_tree_windows_test.go:14-39 covers descendants; sealed build:pose-mcp/go/release-test-compile-windows.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R13-N1\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_tree_windows.go:38-81,115-151 assigns the reviewer while suspended to a kill-on-close job, then terminates and waits for the job; pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_tree_windows_test.go:14-39 covers descendants; sealed build:pose-mcp/go/release-test-compile-windows.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R13-N2\",\n      \"status\": \"partial\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go:12-13 enables the shim for the standard pose command, and pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go:974-991 runs it on Linux. The no-shim path remains at pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go:1112-1116; pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux.go:89-120 scans processes without ancestry, so L6 remains.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R13-N3\",\n      \"status\": \"partial\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim_linux.go:263-285 reads /proc in batches, but :140-173 processes the collected entries without checking the deadline until :189; pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux.go:90-97 also lists and scans without an in-loop deadline.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"sweep\": \"Swept every path listed in the brief and the affected Linux, Windows, and Unix process-tree helpers; dispatch cleanup and run records; attempt reservation, receipt, release, ls/cancel, and round accounting; brief version/digest tests; English and pt-BR manuals and scaffold copies. Checked the listed prior findings. Ran the focused process, release, brief, and interrupted-dispatch tests plus host vet. The strict validate matrix could not create Go work directories in the read-only checkout or /tmp; sealed validation evidence was used for its coverage.\",\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assumption-integrity\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-7d71da6b19af6951\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Verified: the normal Linux CLI enables the isolated shim; its subtree is the adapter run, it reaps children, and the focused regression tests passed. The live-owner release check passed, and release records failed status with a receipt. Unresolved: non-Linux Unix waiting and non-Linux PID reporting (N2/N3), the Linux scan bound (N4), and release recovery across a partial witness publication (N5). Accepted residuals in spec L1/L3/L4/L6 remain explicit; L6 is N1. The Windows descendant test was not executable on this Linux host.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-concurrency\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N2\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The exclusive release lock and live-owner refusal tests pass, but the non-Linux Unix path does not wait for process-group exit; the Linux per-entry scan can also exceed the stated bound (N4).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-contracts\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The cancel option is additive, the run and receipt remain schema version 1, and the entrypoint stays in the existing delegate CLI contract. The delegated-surface integration evidence is sealed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-input-errors\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Attempt ID validation, marker/liveness checks, confirmation for markerless reservations, bounded directory reads, and error returns are covered by the unit suite; focused release tests passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The change touches local review dispatch and delegation storage, not an external service contract. The integration assessment's three unobserved HTTP consumers are unrelated to these changed paths.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-observability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N3\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Linux records reaped PIDs, but the Windows job and non-Linux Unix paths do not populate the ended-process list in safety.limitations.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"compatibility\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-attempt-ledger-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Released attempts retain ordinary v1 failed-run and receipt records; older record readers keep their existing fields and meaning. The confirm-abandoned CLI flag is additive.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"correctness\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N5\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The normal interrupted-dispatch retry path passes, but a release interrupted between run-witness publication and run-record publication leaves history incomplete and the attempt unrecoverable; N2 and N4 also leave R1 gaps.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"design-causality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-7d71da6b19af6951\",\n      \"rationale\": \"D1 addresses escaped-session descendants while isolating subreaper authority in a shim, avoiding the process-wide adoption risk. D2 closes an abandoned reservation with the same failed-run and receipt records old readers consume. The sealed design assessment reports no structural deltas; the remaining issues are implementation coverage gaps.\",\n      \"mappings\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"documentation\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-templates-are-immutable-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The brief uses review-brief/10 and asks commands to finish. English and pt-BR manuals and scaffold copies describe Linux shim, the no-shim fallback, other Unix process groups, Windows jobs, and abandoned-attempt release.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"operability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"delegate ls names stalled causes and the release command; cancel reports the released run and status, and refusal paths give the missing liveness or operator-confirmation condition.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"requirements\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N3\",\n      \"rationale\": \"R3/R4 and the ordinary R5/R6 retry paths have relevant tests, but R1's bounded wait still has platform/scan gaps (N2/N4), R2 lacks ended-PID records outside Linux (N3), and interrupted release publication can still strand R5/R6 (N5).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scope\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-7d71da6b19af6951\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The implementation, CLI, brief, manuals, and generated scaffold copies stay within the spec's listed dispatch, release, and documentation areas; no unrelated behavior was added.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"security\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N1\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The standard Linux CLI uses the subtree shim and skips broad process matching. The no-shim fallback still treats a reviewer-settable environment value as ownership across all same-user PIDs; it can signal an unrelated run.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"solution-proportionality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-7d71da6b19af6951\",\n      \"rationale\": \"A run-scoped subreaper is the smallest sufficient Linux design after a dispatcher-wide subreaper proved too broad; a Windows job is the OS-native equivalent. Group kill alone misses session escapes, while a general process-management framework would add scope without value. The choice is invalidated where non-Linux paths do not wait/report (N2/N3), the Linux scan exceeds its bound (N4), or an embedder uses the settable-environment fallback (N1).\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"artifact-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:$POSE_REVIEW_CLI artifact-check --spec pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes --strict\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran with the sealed CLI and it exited 0. Its report resolved a different change-set head (9636e0ad8e3f6df80ea9b72f2b69bba17b82b936) than this sealed bundle (3e2102bdf778a8af30e5ee38044dfd283488787e), so its 34-claim/40-observed result and warnings were not used to establish this subject's artifact attribution.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-design\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-7d71da6b19af6951\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The no-persist assessment reported no deltas; the sealed structural evidence is pass.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-discover\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:$POSE_REVIEW_CLI assess discover --no-persist --component pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran without persistence and discovered the pose-mcp component.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-integrate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran without persistence. It reported three unobserved HTTP consumers unrelated to the delegate/review paths under review.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:$POSE_REVIEW_CLI assess tech-debt --no-persist\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The scan was incomplete because two existing spec files have unknown scope and it found one uncovered marker. The listed change paths contain no new production TODO/FIXME/stub/panic marker; I did not treat the incomplete repository scan as subject evidence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"closeout-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Deferred until after the review attestation, as required by the tool precondition and the brief's no-attestation boundary.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"review-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Deferred until after the review attestation, as required by the tool precondition and the brief's no-attestation boundary.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"suggest-review\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:$POSE_REVIEW_CLI suggest review --path pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The engine selected backend-go, security, and documentation-style rules; all applicable local rules were read.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"surface-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"reachability:pose-mcp/go/delivery-reachability\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran strict surface-check; it reported one target, 236 results, and zero findings. Sealed reachability evidence is from pose-mcp.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The strict command was attempted, but the sandbox rejected Go build-directory creation in both the checkout and /tmp. The sealed validation matrix includes passing build, e2e, integration, and unit evidence; focused tests and host vet passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The module strict command was attempted and failed only when the read-only sandbox blocked Go build/cache writes. The sealed module matrix includes passing build, e2e, integration, and unit evidence; focused tests and host vet passed.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"}}
